>> title: Miel de Piloncillo
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: piloncillo, syrup, mexican, cinnamon, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: miel de piloncillo, piloncillo syrup, panela syrup, papelón syrup, raw cane sugar syrup, mexican brown sugar syrup
>> pairs-with: puerquitos
>> servings: 12
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — the syrup thickens as it cools, so one boiled hard to look right in the pan sets to a solid in the jar

>> step: simmer 10 min, until the cones dissolve
Simmer @piloncillo cones{8%oz}(225 g; chopped or smashed) in @water{2%cup}(480 mL) ~simmer{10%min}, stirring, until every shard has gone.

>> step: steep the aromatics 15 min off the heat
Draw the pan off the heat, drop @cinnamon stick{1}, @orange peel{2%strip} and @whole cloves{3} into @&(~1)piloncillo syrup{}, and ~steep{15%min} covered.

>> step: strain and cool
Strain @&(~1)steeped syrup{} and let it ~cool{20%min}.
